&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IAM is the nerve center of Stripe. We control how millions of businesses grant access to their account, including employees, AI agents, apps, and API integrations, across the Dashboard, API, CLI, and MCP. We&#39;re also a platform team, building the unified, fine-grained permissions model that every product at Stripe builds on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI agents are changing how businesses operate, and how they get authorized, governed, and secured is being defined right now—largely by us. We build for solo founders and Fortune 500s alike, and the tension between those two is where the real product work lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll set the vision and drive the roadmap for how every principal, human, agent, or app, gets access to a Stripe account. You&#39;ll do it by talking directly to the founders, admins, and developers who use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design the experience of granting access, everywhere.&lt;/strong&gt; Signing up, inviting a teammate, creating an API key, authorizing an agent or a third-party app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make agents a first-class citizen.&lt;/strong&gt; Define how agents authenticate, what they&#39;re allowed to do, and how businesses stay in control, including approvals and human-in-the-loop checkpoints for the actions that matter most. You&#39;re defining an experience that will set the industry standard.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive least privilege, made easy.&lt;/strong&gt; Build custom roles, smart permission defaults, and usage-based recommendations that make the secure choice the obvious one instead of the tedious one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Push toward a world without secrets.&lt;/strong&gt; Make secretless authentication (Workload Identity Federation) the default way developers integrate with Stripe, eliminating API key leaks as a category of risk rather than reducing their blast radius.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across nearly all of Stripe.&lt;/strong&gt; Pitch an ambitious vision, then get teams across Dashboard, API Platform, Security, Payments and Money Movement genuinely excited to build it with you, even though none of them report to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship, learn, and iterate: &lt;/strong&gt;Run experiments, follow real usage, and adjust quickly rather than waiting for the perfect plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hardest part of this job, and the most fun, is the constant trade-off: usability vs. security, flexibility vs. simplicity. It takes taste to find a shape that feels effortless for a solo founder and holds up at Fortune 500 scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product management, shipping platform or infrastructure products that other teams build on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in security, identity, auth, or developer platforms, or serious curiosity about the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of talking to users to find the real problem, not the reported one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineers on authorization and authentication design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward experimentation over big-bang launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort setting direction in a space that&#39;s still being invented, across teams you don&#39;t manage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Growth organization drives Stripe&#39;s self-serve growth engine: from a user&#39;s first interaction with Stripe through onboarding, activation, and expansion across our products. Growth focuses on building the systems and surfaces that help any user find, understand, and adopt the right set of Stripe products, regardless of how or where they start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Growth, the onboarding program is how new and existing users get to their first successful use of Stripe as quickly and completely as possible. A cohesive onboarding experience is critical to Stripe&#39;s ability to convert prospects, activate new products, and compete against increasingly sophisticated alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onboarding spans several interconnected surfaces:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquisition and intent capture — first-touch experiences that match prospects to the right products and entry points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account setup and activation — guided flows that get users live with the right integration shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-product discovery — contextual surfaces that help new and existing users adopt additional products over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These surfaces are deeply interdependent, span dozens of cross-functional teams, and directly shape Stripe&#39;s new user activation and product attach rates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are seeking a product-focused Technical Program Manager to drive Stripe&#39;s onboarding programs. This is a high-impact role at the intersection of growth strategy, product management, and cross-organizational program ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In this role, you will own one of the most strategically consequential programs in Growth, driving the direction, health, and outcomes of Stripe&#39;s onboarding experience end-to-end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will set the program strategy in partnership with Growth leadership, holding organizations accountable to the success of the program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-org decisions across DRIs in Growth, Dashboard, Docs, Marketing, and product teams actively resolving the hard, ambiguous integration and ownership questions that fall between team boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and shape product and engineering roadmaps bringing a program-level perspective to team planning cycles, and advocating for cross-cutting investments that no single team will prioritize on their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program management experience with demonstrated success in driving complex cross organizational programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and ability to understand enterprise customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to communicate with precision and credibility across engineering, product, and executive audiences, translating complex technical trade-offs into strategic decisions, and driving alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead and align cross-functional teams — driving decisions, resolving conflict, and building consensus across organizations with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successful program delivery in complex technical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in product management or product operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

